endobj

593 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 242 0 R/T(I checked this on the generated data. In the 100-lender population 74 of 140 persons share their full name with someone else. In the 1,000-lender population it is 1,036 of 1,040, and the most common name \("Asha Khan"\) occurs 12 times. The generator draws names from short lists on purpose so this problem is visible, but real museums have the same problem with common names. A name also changes after marriage or for a trust that is renamed. )/E(I checked this on the generated data. In the 100-lender population 74 of 140 persons share their full name with someone else. In the 1,000-lender population it is 1,036 of 1,040, and the most common name \("Asha Khan"\) occurs 12 times. The generator draws names from short lists on purpose so this problem is visible, but real museums have the same problem with common names. A name also changes after marriage or for a trust that is renamed. )/Pg 24 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

594 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 242 0 R/T(How concurrent registration avoids duplicate identifiers )/E(How concurrent registration avoids duplicate identifiers )/Pg 24 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

595 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 242 0 R/T(Two registrars may register a new artifact at the same moment. If the application did SELECT MAX\(artifact_id\)+1, both would read the same maximum and both would try to insert the same number. The DBMS must issue the numbers instead. )/E(Two registrars may register a new artifact at the same moment. If the application did SELECT MAX\(artifact_id\)+1, both would read the same maximum and both would try to insert the same number. The DBMS must issue the numbers instead. )/Pg 24 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

596 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 242 0 R/T(Why an exhibition name cannot identify a display slot )/E(Why an exhibition name cannot identify a display slot )/Pg 24 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

597 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 242 0 R/T(Meridian can run "Bronze Age Treasures" in 2025 and again in 2027, and an exhibition can be renamed after it opens. "Bronze Age Treasures / slot 7" would then point to two different physical places, or to none after a rename. The numeric exhibition_id never changes, so the key \(exhibition_id, slot_no\) stays valid. )/E(Meridian can run "Bronze Age Treasures" in 2025 and again in 2027, and an exhibition can be renamed after it opens. "Bronze Age Treasures / slot 7" would then point to two different physical places, or to none after a rename. The numeric exhibition_id never changes, so the key \(exhibition_id, slot_no\) stays valid. )/Pg 24 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

