673 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 245 0 R/T(What I use instead: the three-way fact is not a fact in itself in Meridian. It is the result of an independent LOAN. Each loan has exactly one lender and one handling curator, and its objects are placed in slots of exhibitions. With loan_id as the join key the spurious tuple cannot appear: loans 100 \(Raman, Divya, E1\), 101 \(Raman, Karthik, E2\), 102 \(Asha, Divya, E2\) join back to exactly three tuples, because loan_id is a key of every projection. So the model keeps binary associations and lets LOAN carry the connection. )/E(What I use instead: the three-way fact is not a fact in itself in Meridian. It is the result of an independent LOAN. Each loan has exactly one lender and one handling curator, and its objects are placed in slots of exhibitions. With loan_id as the join key the spurious tuple cannot appear: loans 100 \(Raman, Divya, E1\), 101 \(Raman, Karthik, E2\), 102 \(Asha, Divya, E2\) join back to exactly three tuples, because loan_id is a key of every projection. So the model keeps binary associations and lets LOAN carry the connection. )/Pg 27 0 R/K[25]>>
endobj

