805 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 251 0 R/T(Every entity in the Task 2 catalog appears in the diagram or in the EER figure. The diagram keeps LENDER, CURATOR and REGISTRAR as separate boxes only so that the loan and report paths stay readable; their common supertype PERSON, with its name, e-mail and phone attributes, is drawn once in the EER \(Task 5\) instead of being repeated three times here. For the same reason ARTIFACT and LOAN are drawn again as repeated references in the EER of Task 12; they are the same entities, only reused to show the ownership addition. The custody and condition-evidence cardinalities annotated on the lines are the ones defended in Task 3: a loan has at least one line \(double line on CONTAINS\), a report must have its line \(double line on EVIDENCED_BY\) but a line may have no report \(single line on the LOAN_OBJECT side\). )/E(Every entity in the Task 2 catalog appears in the diagram or in the EER figure. The diagram keeps LENDER, CURATOR and REGISTRAR as separate boxes only so that the loan and report paths stay readable; their common supertype PERSON, with its name, e-mail and phone attributes, is drawn once in the EER \(Task 5\) instead of being repeated three times here. For the same reason ARTIFACT and LOAN are drawn again as repeated references in the EER of Task 12; they are the same entities, only reused to show the ownership addition. The custody and condition-evidence cardinalities annotated on the lines are the ones defended in Task 3: a loan has at least one line \(double line on CONTAINS\), a report must have its line \(double line on EVIDENCED_BY\) but a line may have no report \(single line on the LOAN_OBJECT side\). )/Pg 33 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

