842 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 253 0 R/T(When a loan is overdue the museum notifies a contact, and that contact can be either a person \(the lender or an agent\) or an organization \(a shipping or fine-art agent\). PERSON and ORGANIZATION have different keys and attributes, so neither is a subtype of the other. NOTIFICATION_CONTACT is therefore a category: each contact is exactly one of PERSON or ORGANIZATION. It gets its own surrogate contact_id, and a row-level CHECK makes sure exactly one of person_id and org_id is filled. This can be enforced with a CHECK and it was tested \(Task 8\). )/E(When a loan is overdue the museum notifies a contact, and that contact can be either a person \(the lender or an agent\) or an organization \(a shipping or fine-art agent\). PERSON and ORGANIZATION have different keys and attributes, so neither is a subtype of the other. NOTIFICATION_CONTACT is therefore a category: each contact is exactly one of PERSON or ORGANIZATION. It gets its own surrogate contact_id, and a row-level CHECK makes sure exactly one of person_id and org_id is filled. This can be enforced with a CHECK and it was tested \(Task 8\). )/Pg 35 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

843 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 253 0 R/T(5.3 How the discriminator controls membership )/E(5.3 How the discriminator controls membership )/Pg 35 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

844 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 253 0 R/T(emp_role is the discriminator. A row with emp_role = CURATOR is a curator and may handle loans; a row with REGISTRAR may file condition reports. Because the value is single, the subtypes cannot overlap. The link to custody and evidence is direct: LOAN.curator_id should point only to curators, and CONDITION_REPORT.registrar_id only to registrars. The column CHECK limits emp_role to three allowed values, but it cannot check the role of the row that a foreign key points to. That is a cross-table rule and I test it in Task 8 \(probe 1\). )/E(emp_role is the discriminator. A row with emp_role = CURATOR is a curator and may handle loans; a row with REGISTRAR may file condition reports. Because the value is single, the subtypes cannot overlap. The link to custody and evidence is direct: LOAN.curator_id should point only to curators, and CONDITION_REPORT.registrar_id only to registrars. The column CHECK limits emp_role to three allowed values, but it cannot check the role of the row that a foreign key points to. That is a cross-table rule and I test it in Task 8 \(probe 1\). )/Pg 35 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

