<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 282 0 R/T(In a hierarchical model every record has exactly one parent. Thenatural root is LENDER, with LOAN below it and the loan objects below the loan. The handling curator is a second parent of LOAN, which a tree cannot express, so the curator record is copied under each loan \(the red copy in the figure\) or reached through a pointer outside the tree. )/E(In a hierarchical model every record has exactly one parent. Thenatural root is LENDER, with LOAN below it and the loan objects below the loan. The handling curator is a second parent of LOAN, which a tree cannot express, so the curator record is copied under each loan \(the red copy in the figure\) or reached through a pointer outside the tree. )/Pg 64 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

1544 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 282 0 R/T(In a network \(CODASYL-style\) model a record can be a member of several sets, so LOANis a member of LENDER_LOAN and CURATOR_LOAN at the same time. This removes the duplicate curator. The price is navigation: the program has to walk the sets record by record \(find owner, find next member\). )/E(In a network \(CODASYL-style\) model a record can be a member of several sets, so LOANis a member of LENDER_LOAN and CURATOR_LOAN at the same time. This removes the duplicate curator. The price is navigation: the program has to walk the sets record by record \(find owner, find next member\). )/Pg 64 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

