<</Title(The new requirement says custody must stay distinct from ownership history. In this design the two are physically separate: loan, loan_object, condition_report and placement have no ownership column, and the migration changed none of their rows. Only the table that answers "who owns it, in what share, from when" is new. That is why the right response is to modify the model and not to redesign it: the keys and relations that carry custody periods and condition evidence stay the same, and the added cost is one association, one index and three verification queries.)/Dest[78 0 R/Fit]/Parent 3965 0 R>>
endobj

