<</Title(Counterexample from this case. Lender 1017 sends artifacts 11 and 14 on 1 September 2026 under one agreement with curator Divya. In A the museum stores two LOAN rows \(1017, 11, 2026-09-01\) and \(1017, 14, 2026-09-01\). The curator and the end date are repeated, and nothing records that the two rows are one loan. If the same lender sends artifact 11 again on the same day under a second agreement, the key \(1017, 11, 2026-09-01\) collides. An independent LOAN entity solves both: loan 100 holds both artifacts and loan 101 is a separate occurrence.)/Dest[19 0 R/Fit]/Parent 4103 0 R/Prev 4120 0 R/Next 4121 0 R>>
