4378 0 obj
<</Title(Binary projections: LC = {\(Raman, Divya\), \(Raman, Karthik\), \(Asha, Divya\)}, CE = {\(Divya, E1\), \(Karthik, E2\), \(Divya, E2\)}, LE = {\(Raman, E1\), \(Raman, E2\), \(Asha, E2\)}. Join LC with CE on curator, then with LE on \(lender, exhibition\). The result has four tuples: t1, t2, t3 and the extra tuple \(Raman, Divya, E2\). That tuple was never in T. It says Divya handled a Raman loan in E2, which never happened, and it would wrongly create a custody period and a condition-report duty. So the three-way fact cannot be rebuilt from binary relationships, and the ternary relationship cannot simply be split.)/Dest[26 0 R/Fit]/Parent 4368 0 R/Next 4391 0 R>>
endobj

