4413 0 obj
<</Title(In a hierarchical model every record has exactly one parent. Thenatural root is LENDER, with LOAN below it and the loan objects below the loan. The handling curator is a second parent of LOAN, which a tree cannot express, so the curator record is copied under each loan \(the red copy in the figure\) or reached through a pointer outside the tree.)/Dest[64 0 R/Fit]/Parent 4381 0 R/Prev 4396 0 R/Next 4427 0 R>>
endobj

4414 0 obj
<</Title(In a network \(CODASYL-style\) model a record can be a member of several sets, so LOANis a member of LENDER_LOAN and CURATOR_LOAN at the same time. This removes the duplicate curator. The price is navigation: the program has to walk the sets record by record \(find owner, find next member\).)/Dest[64 0 R/Fit]/Parent 4381 0 R/Prev 4427 0 R/Next 4397 0 R>>
endobj

4415 0 obj
<</Title(> SLOT is a)/Dest[66 0 R/Fit]/Parent 4351 0 R/Prev 4401 0 R/Next 4428 0 R>>
