4786 0 obj
<</Title(Every entity in the Task 2 catalog appears in the diagram or in the EER figure. The diagram keeps LENDER, CURATOR and REGISTRAR as separate boxes only so that the loan and report paths stay readable; their common supertype PERSON, with its name, e-mail and phone attributes, is drawn once in the EER \(Task 5\) instead of being repeated three times here. For the same reason ARTIFACT and LOAN are drawn again as repeated references in the EER of Task 12; they are the same entities, only reused to show the ownership addition. The custody and condition-evidence cardinalities annotated on the lines are the ones defended in Task 3: a loan has at least one line \(double line on CONTAINS\), a report must have its line \(double line on EVIDENCED_BY\) but a line may have no report \(single line on the LOAN_OBJECT side\).)/Dest[33 0 R/Fit]/Parent 4777 0 R>>
endobj

4787 0 obj
<</Title(A curator can be a lender at the same)/Dest[34 0 R/Fit]/Parent 4770 0 R/Prev 4778 0 R/Next 4796 0 R>>
endobj

4788 0 obj
<</Title(PERSON to LENDER/EMPLOYEE is total. Every person in the register is at least a lender or an employee \(the person_kind column records which: LENDER, EMPLOYEE or BOTH\).)/Dest[34 0 R/Fit]/Parent 4770 0 R/Prev 4796 0 R/Next 4779 0 R>>
endobj

4789 0 obj
<</Title(emp_role is the discriminator. A row with emp_role = CURATOR is a curator and may handle loans; a row with REGISTRAR may file condition reports. Because the value is single, the subtypes cannot overlap. The link to custody and evidence is direct: LOAN.curator_id should point only to curators, and CONDITION_REPORT.registrar_id only to registrars. The column CHECK limits emp_role to three allowed values, but it cannot check the role of the row that a foreign key points to. That is a cross-table rule and I test it in Task 8 \(probe 1\).)/Dest[35 0 R/Fit]/Parent 4780 0 R>>
endobj

4790 0 obj
<</Title(5.4 Notification contact as a category \(union\))/Dest[35 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 4780 0 R/First 4797 0 R/Last 4798 0 R/Count -2/Next 4799 0 R>>
endobj

