4796 0 obj
<</Title(time. This is real in the generated data: query Q8 in Task 9 returns 3 curators who also lend.)/Dest[34 0 R/Fit]/Parent 4770 0 R/Prev 4787 0 R/Next 4788 0 R>>
endobj

4797 0 obj
<</Title(When a loan is overdue the museum notifies a contact, and that contact can be either a person \(the lender or an agent\) or an organization \(a shipping or fine-art agent\). PERSON and ORGANIZATION have different keys and attributes, so neither is a subtype of the other. NOTIFICATION_CONTACT is therefore a category: each contact is exactly one of PERSON or ORGANIZATION. It gets its own surrogate contact_id, and a row-level CHECK makes sure exactly one of person_id and org_id is filled. This can be enforced with a CHECK and it was tested \(Task 8\).)/Dest[35 0 R/Fit]/Parent 4790 0 R/Next 4798 0 R>>
endobj

